cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the stimuli, the result tables, or the code in this repository,
  please cite it as below.
title: >-
  Where Do Semantics Live? A Homonym-Based Study of Semantic Disambiguation in
  Large Language Models (code, stimuli and processed results)
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hagen
    given-names: Julia
    affiliation: Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jihagen/LLM_Homonym_Semantics"
url: "https://github.com/Jihagen/LLM_Homonym_Semantics"
abstract: >-
  Code, stimuli and processed results for a study of contextual word-sense
  information in the hidden states of four bidirectional encoders and four
  causal decoders, using seven two-sense English homonyms. The release
  supports reproduction of all report figures from compact result tables and
  documents how to rerun the models.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - semantic representations
  - homonyms
  - word sense disambiguation
  - representational geometry
  - layer selection
references:
  - type: report
    title: >-
      Where Do Semantics Live? A Homonym-Based Study of Semantic
      Disambiguation in Large Language Models
    authors:
